~ initialize_local_variables

=> start

~ start
...[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_stairs")][wait=9]
Shopkeeper: [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_open")]Morning, there. I see you're itching to get started. Sleep well?
- Morning. Slept just fine. 
	Shopkeeper: Good. Wouldn't want you tired on your first day. Especially after such a long journey.[do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "know", true)]
	- How do you know so much about me already?
		Shopkeeper: Your arrival was heralded by the Elders.
		Shopkeeper: They told of someone bearing the Gift who would soon come help me around with the shop. Goddess knows I could use it. 
		Shopkeeper: To be honest, though, you never know with them. Their predictions have been wrong just as often as they've been right. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]...Make sure not to tell anyone I said that, please. 
		Shopkeeper: I've got my own connection with the Goddess, though. She told me what I needed to know Herself.
		- I see. 
			Shopkeeper: Alright then. Let's get you up to speed, eh? => tutorial
		- She talked to me, too. In my sleep, in what felt like a dream. Told me to come here. 
			Shopkeeper: I'm well aware. She rarely does that, you know. 
			- Any idea why She chose me?
				Shopkeeper: None. She's not exactly straightforward, our Goddess. Gods rarely are.
				Shopkeeper: All I know is you're important to her, and she wants me to train you. And for you to help me.
				Shopkeeper: And that's all I need to know for now.
				- Fair enough.
					Shopkeeper: Let's get you started, then. => tutorial 
				- I'll need a bit more than that.
					Shopkeeper: I'll explain everything, don't worry. => tutorial
			- Anyway. Let's get to work. 
				Shopkeeper: Let's. => tutorial 
		- Who are these "Elders"? 
			Shopkeeper: They're the founders and leaders of our wonderful village and church. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "elders", true)]
			Shopkeeper: They're the only ones who can communicate directly with the Goddess, besides me, of course. 
			Shopkeeper: They're very old, hence the name. They rarely come out of their home. They have underlings and messengers in their service, and that's how they usually communicate the Goddess's will and teachings to the rest of us.
			Shopkeeper: There's a chance you won't ever see them yourself, but it's safer to assume they're aware of your every move. 
			Shopkeeper: They don't take kindly to meddling newcomers. And they're not known for being forgiving to heretics and blasphemers. 
			Shopkeeper: Since you're not technically part of our church yet, the most severe form of punishment you could undergo is exile. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]But once you take the oath and become a fully fledged member, the punishment for sinning is either flogging, or death, depending on the severity of your actions. 
			Shopkeeper: Sounds worse than it is. All you have to do is not speak against or openly defy our Goddess. 
			- Sounds simple enough.
				Shopkeeper: It is. 
				Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's's get you up to speed, eh? => tutorial
			- That's... fucked up. 
				Shopkeeper: Salvation comes at a cost.[do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)][do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)]
				Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's's get you up to speed, eh? => tutorial
	- Yeah. I'm just eager to start working, to be honest. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 5]
		Shopkeeper: A man after my own heart. => tutorial
	- Yeah. I'm just eager to start serving the Goddess, to be honest. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >= 6]
		Shopkeeper: I see. No point mucking about, then. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)][do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)] => tutorial
	- Guess not. Got a bunch of questions, though.
		Shopkeeper: Of course. And I'll answer each and every one of them, as best I can. => tutorial
- Not really. Got a lot on my mind.
	Shopkeeper: Care to share? [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "cult", true)]
	- Not right now, to be honest.
		Shopkeeper: No worries. Just know I'm here if you wanna talk. And I'm mostly an open book, if you've got any questions. 
		Shopkeeper: Gotta stick together, us so favoured by the Goddess, eh? People can get as jealous here as anywhere else.
		- Of course.
			Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's get you up to speed, eh? => tutorial
		- Let's just get to work. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Alright then. Let's get started. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", -1)] => tutorial 
	- Yeah. Kind of feels like I'm joining a cult. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 6]
		Shopkeeper: Eh, people here are just like everywhere else. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)]
		Shopkeeper: Some good apples, some bad ones. Perhaps a few rotten ones here and there. 
		Shopkeeper: There are some practices and beliefs which might seem... odd, especially to an outsider.
		Shopkeeper: Way I see it, at least they've got a purpose.
		Shopkeeper: Goes a long way, what with the state of the world right now and everything.
		- Guess I can respect that. 
			Shopkeeper: Just keep an open mind, yeah? 
			Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's get you up to speed. => tutorial
		- Still feels weird. 
			Shopkeeper: I get it. I do. Just give it a bit of time. You've got me to help you settle in and answer all your questions.[do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", -1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", 1)] => tutorial
	- The way you greeted me last night creeped me out. Like you were already expecting me. 
		Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Oh, well, uh, I kind of was. I'm sorry if that was weird. [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_4", "wait", true)]
		Shopkeeper: Been working alone ever since I came here. Hasn't been ideal, but I got used to it. Forgot how to behave around people, seems like. 
		Shopkeeper: It's just that I've known for a while someone bearing the Gift would come, and yesterday I felt this urge to look out the window right before you came into view.
		Shopkeeper: And there you were. As soon as I saw you, I somehow knew it was you. Can't explain it any more than that, though I wish I could.
		Shopkeeper: Plus, I didn't want your knocking to wake Sarah up, truth be told. She's a light sleeper. 
		Shopkeeper: I'll try to be less spooky from now on, though. Promise. 
		- To be honest, I, myself, kind of knew this was your house even before Joan pointed it to me.
			Shopkeeper: There you have it. The Goddess works in ways unknown to us. 
			Shopkeeper: Let's get started, then. => tutorial
		- No harm, no foul. 
			Shopkeeper: Appreciate it. Let's get started, then. => tutorial
		- Err, not sure how I feel about that. 
			Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]I know, I'm being odd again. But it's the truth.
			- Just tone it down a bit, yeah?
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Duly noted. Already said I would. [do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "relationship", -1)]
				Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's get started. => tutorial
			- Guess I gotta get used to it, then. 
				Shopkeeper: [#sprite=worried]Like I said, I'll try to make it easier on you. 
				Shopkeeper: Anyway, let's get started. => tutorial
	- Just eager to start serving the Goddess. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >= 6]
		Shopkeeper: Oh, no point mucking about, then. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)][do Variables.mod_char_var("NPC_4", "express_doubt", -1)] => tutorial
